 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? Panniers on the front and rear rack on the frame are the simplest and safest. Backpacks and shoulder bags can get heavy and lean the bike. Baskets add a lot of drag, and they' easily tipped over in corners. For short trips, a backpack works fine. Then a backpack is fine, just take your time and stop often. A small shop on the corner is cheaper than bike shop. It can feel heavy if the shopping is heavy and you' not used to it. A small front pannier helps lot.",
